# Build-context exclusions (KI-57).
#
# Every deployments/compose/*.yml builds with `context: ../..`, i.e. the
# whole repository, and Docker deliberately ignores .gitignore. Without this
# file the context carried real private keys, the step-ca provisioner
# password, and the entire .git history into BuildKit's cache - material that
# the multi-stage builds keep out of the FINAL images but not out of an
# intermediate stage, which `--target build`, `--cache-to`, or a `docker save`
# of that stage publishes verbatim (RD-01, PKI-F-02).
#
# What the builds actually need from the context, verified against every
# COPY in deployments/docker/*/Dockerfile: go.mod, go.sum, the Go module
# source (pkg/, services/, test/, user-client/ - all pulled in by the build
# stages' `COPY . .`), services/{database-vault,metrics-collector}/migrations,
# and deployments/docker/<service>/{rootfs/,sshd_config,nginx.conf}. Nothing
# below is referenced by any COPY, and no Go package uses go:embed, so
# nothing here can be reached at build time.

# Version-control and agent/tooling state (also the largest single item).
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
graphify-out
.obsidian
.vscode
.idea

# Third-party runtime config and dev-only PKI material: mounted into
# containers as volumes at RUN time by deployments/compose/*.yml, never
# COPYed at BUILD time. Holds Mosquitto's issued private keys, Headscale's
# dev TLS key, Entry-Hub's server key, and step-ca's provisioner password.
third-party

# Documentation and static assets: no COPY, no go:embed.
docs
assets
private
**/*.md
LICENSE

# Belt-and-braces: no Dockerfile COPYs any key, certificate, or env file.
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
**/*.dev-only.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
